    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d886">

                <pb facs="1023" n="927" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg927"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860j.48/80</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-02-09"><hi rendition="#italic">February 9,
                        1921</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received March 1.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 42</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In previous despatches<anchor n="47"
                        xml:id="d886-f1"/> I have reported regarding the withdrawal of the Near East
                    Relief from Armenian territory under Bolshevik occupation, and have communicated
                    the minutes of meetings held between representatives of the Near East Relief and
                    the <pb facs="1024" n="928" xml:id="pg928"/> Bolshevik Commissary at
                    Alexandropol. I now have the honor to submit a copy of a letter addressed on
                    January 4th to the Commissary of Alexandropol, by Dr. E. A. Yarrow, director of
                    the Caucasus branch of the Near East Relief, summarizing the reasons for the
                    withdrawal of relief work from Bolshevik territory.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mark L. Bristol</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d886-a1.xml" xpointer="d886-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
